A macro declared as a real argv command under `core.macros` (not a `macro_stubs`
entry) executes through the CLI subprocess boundary: `echo 1` writes its actual
output `1` into the frontmatter, proving live macro execution.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    echo_one:
      - echo
      - "1"
-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md 'key={{ macro("core.macros.echo_one") }}'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
+key: 1
 ---
 # Body
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: key=1
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
key: 1
---
# Body
